  "output": {
    "svg": "architecture.svg",
    "medium": "documentation and notebook",
    "alt_text": "An agent proposes only archive and program identifiers while authenticated application context supplies identity and tenant. Archive admission canonicalizes paths and rejects links, special files, collisions, and oversized content. A broker binds current policy, image, input, and program digests into a one-use grant. A disposable runtime enforces exact filesystem roots, resource budgets, default-deny network and syscall policy, validates bounded output, emits redacted receipts, and destroys the workspace on every terminal path."
